From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:30:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] keybindings: let accelerator grabs stay active while an app
 inhibits shortcuts

A game clipper binds a shortcut through the global shortcuts portal so
the person can save a clip while playing. Games that hold the keyboard,
such as an Xwayland game granted its keyboard grab, inhibit shortcuts,
and every accelerator grab was skipped then: the inhibition check read
only the flags of the shared external-grab handler, so
META_KEY_BINDING_NON_MASKABLE passed to meta_display_grab_accelerator()
had no effect.

The check now honours NON_MASKABLE on the binding as well as on its
handler, so the shell can keep the accelerators the person approved for
an app active over a game while its own shortcuts stay inhibitable.

Upstream-Status: luft-only GNOME Shell offers no global shortcuts portal that would need it
---
 src/core/keybindings.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/core/keybindings.c b/src/core/keybindings.c
index 70eee5716022b51db5f4e2137b13785e55336b43..936e67ec8fee87d22a9578afa259580bf531529e 100644
--- a/src/core/keybindings.c
+++ b/src/core/keybindings.c
@@ -1484,7 +1484,7 @@ process_event (MetaDisplay          *display,
     goto not_found;
 
   if (display->focus_window &&
-      !(binding->handler->flags & META_KEY_BINDING_NON_MASKABLE))
+      !((binding->flags | binding->handler->flags) & META_KEY_BINDING_NON_MASKABLE))
     {
       ClutterInputDevice *source;
 
